FILE: app/src/set-share.ts
```ts
import type { AnimationManager, AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { setAnimationWeight, fadeAnimationWeight } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function setShareNow(manager: AnimationManager, group: AnimationGroup, share: number): void {
    setAnimationWeight(group, share);
    fadeAnimationWeight(manager, group, { to: share, durationMs: 0, from: share });
}
```

I set the weight immediately via `setAnimationWeight`, then call `fadeAnimationWeight` with a zero-duration fade from `share` to `share` — per the notes, a new fade on the same group replaces any existing one, so this cancels whatever fade was under way, and the zero-duration fade is a no-op that leaves the weight at `share` on every subsequent frame. I'm slightly unsure whether the library's zero-duration fade task removes itself after the first update or lingers as a harmless no-op, but either way the weight stays correct and a later `fadeAnimationWeight` call will replace it as usual.
